<!--
  Approval pickup. Runs scripts/triage-approve.sh at 13:00 and 17:00 local time,
  Monday to Thursday. If the Mac is asleep at that moment, launchd runs the job on
  wake. The 08:30 morning run also picks up approvals, so this covers the rest of the day.

  What an unattended run may send: it posts replies in the digest thread only
  (acknowledgements and job results); it posts no new digest, sends no email and
  replies to no one else. It starts at most 3 background builds for tasks the owner
  approved with `go`, once builds are enabled; they never push or deploy. Tools are limited to .claude/triage/allowed-tools.txt. To pause it without
  uninstalling:
    touch .claude/triage/triage.off

  NOT INSTALLED BY DEFAULT. Install only after a manual dry run looks right:
    TRIAGE_ARGS="--dry-run" bash scripts/triage-approve.sh

  Install:
    cp scripts/triage-approve.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/io.teamzissou.triage-approve.plist
    launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/io.teamzissou.triage-approve.plist

  Run it once, right now:
    launchctl start io.teamzissou.triage-approve

  Uninstall:
    launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/io.teamzissou.triage-approve.plist
    rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/io.teamzissou.triage-approve.plist

  Each run's report lands in .claude/triage/reports/{date}-approve-{HHMM}.md.
  Run output and errors are appended to ~/Library/Logs/triage-approve.log
-->
